{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30253 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "Amurensin appears to exert its biological effects through a shared target, Caspase-5, which is involved in multiple downstream pathways. The evidence suggests that Amurensin acts as a target for Caspase-5, which in turn is targeted by several compounds, including 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid and Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate. These compounds are all implicated in the regulation of Replicase polyprotein 1ab, a key component of the viral life cycle. The integration of these pathways implies that Amurensin may influence the viral replication process through the activation or inhibition of Caspase-5, which could modulate the activity of the replicase polyprotein. The consistent targeting of Caspase-5 across different compounds supports a mechanism where Amurensin interacts with the viral machinery via this common intermediate, highlighting a potential role in viral pathogenesis.",
